 "notes": "95% CL upper limit on g_agamma (red 'Sgr A*' curve in Fig. 1, combined three EHT sub-array data sets from day 82 of the Sgr A* polarimetric observations of ref. [51]). Curve traced from the vector paths of e-print figure polarization_v1.pdf; y-axis calibrated with tick-label positions and validated against the SN1987A line (5.3e-12 GeV^-1); x-axis anchored to the paper's stated mass scan of 1e-20 to 1e-17 eV (Sec. 3), which matches the curve's exact 3.000-decade span. The limit assumes a solitonic core + NFW dark-matter profile at the Galactic center (source density ~1e8 GeV/cm^3, Eqs. 2.9/2.12), not the local DM density, so no rescaling to rho=0.45 GeV/cm^3 applies. The jagged jumps are real features discussed in the paper (phi_bkg degeneracy at low mass; non-significant preferred regions at high mass, best-fit TS=21.7 at ma=7.9e-18 eV, gag=3.2e-11 GeV^-1, excluded by other probes).",
